---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import Comparison from '../components/Comparison.astro';
import Calculator from '../components/Calculator.astro';
import samples from '../data/samples.json';
import cameras from '../data/cameras.json';
import {calculateStorage} from '../data/storage.mjs';
export function getStaticPaths(){return cameras.map(camera=>({params:{camera:samples.find(s=>s.id===camera.sampleId)!.slug+'-raw-vs-jpeg'},props:{camera}}));}
const {camera}=Astro.props;
const sample=samples.find(s=>s.id===camera.sampleId)!;
const mb=sample.rawBytes/1e6;
const estimate=(photos:number,format:string)=>calculateStorage({rawMB:mb,jpegMB:8,photos,format,cardGB:128,copies:2,drivePrice:80,driveTB:2,cloudPerTB:60});
const gb=(value:number)=>value.toLocaleString('en-US',{maximumFractionDigits:1});
const related=cameras.filter(c=>c.sampleId!==camera.sampleId);
const capacity=[32,64,128,256,512,1024];
const cardCount=(gb:number,format:'raw'|'jpeg'|'both')=>Math.floor(gb*1e9/(sample.rawBytes+(format==='raw'?0:format==='jpeg'?-sample.rawBytes+8e6:8e6)));
const faqSchema={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage",mainEntity:camera.questions.map(q=>({"@type":"Question",name:q.question,acceptedAnswer:{"@type":"Answer",text:q.answer}}))};
const breadcrumbSchema={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList",itemListElement:[{"@type":"ListItem",position:1,name:"Home",item:"https://raw-vs-jpeg.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem",position:2,name:"Cameras",item:"https://raw-vs-jpeg.com/cameras/"},{"@type":"ListItem",position:3,name:camera.name,item:`https://raw-vs-jpeg.com/${sample.slug}-raw-vs-jpeg/`}]};
const articleSchema={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article",headline:`${camera.name} RAW file size: measured sample and storage`,mainEntityOfPage:`https://raw-vs-jpeg.com/${sample.slug}-raw-vs-jpeg/`,author:{"@type":"Organization",name:"RAW vs JPEG",url:"https://raw-vs-jpeg.com/about/"},publisher:{"@type":"Organization",name:"RAW vs JPEG"},isBasedOn:sample.url};
const jsonLD=[breadcrumbSchema,articleSchema,faqSchema];
---
<Layout title={`${camera.name} RAW File Size: Measured Sample & Storage`} description={`Measured ${camera.name} RAW sample size, 32 GB–1 TB card estimates, JPEG comparison and original file source. Calculate how many photos fit.`} jsonLD={jsonLD}>
<section class="hero wrap camera-hero"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/cameras/">Cameras</a> / <span aria-current="page">{camera.name}</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">CAMERA FIELD NOTES / {sample.brand.toUpperCase()}</p><h1>{camera.shortName}.<br/><span>Which files should you keep?</span></h1><div class="hero-bottom"><p>{camera.intro}</p><a class="primary-button" href="#storage">Calculate my storage ↓</a></div><div class="camera-stats"><div><strong>{mb.toFixed(2)} MB</strong><span>One measured RAW sample</span></div><div><strong>{Math.floor(128000/mb).toLocaleString('en-US')}</strong><span>Sample-sized RAW files / 128 GB</span></div><div><strong>{gb(estimate(10000,'raw').annualGB)} GB</strong><span>10,000 sample-sized RAW files</span></div></div><p class="sample-mode">{camera.modeLabel} · <a href={sample.url}>View the CC0 source ↗</a></p></section>
<Comparison sampleId={camera.sampleId}/>
<section class="wrap prose compact"><h2>A measured sample, not a camera average.</h2><p>{camera.note}</p><h2>How many {camera.shortName} photos fit on a memory card?</h2><p>For a camera using this exact RAW sample size, the following are theoretical maximums calculated from the original file's {sample.rawBytes.toLocaleString('en-US')} bytes. JPEG assumes 8 MB per shot, and RAW + JPEG adds that assumed JPEG. Actual results depend on your image content, camera settings and formatted card capacity.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Estimated photographs by memory card size, decimal capacity, before overhead</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Card</th><th scope="col">RAW (measured size)</th><th scope="col">JPEG (estimated size)</th><th scope="col">RAW + JPEG (estimated)</th></tr></thead><tbody>{capacity.map(size=><tr><th scope="row">{size===1024?'1 TB':size+' GB'}</th><td>{cardCount(size,'raw').toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td>{cardCount(size,'jpeg').toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td>{cardCount(size,'both').toLocaleString('en-US')}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><h2>Which RAW mode does this camera sample represent?</h2><p>{camera.note} This is one specific capture, not a measurement of every compression setting. Check the original <a href={sample.url}>CC0 RAW source file</a> and its published SHA-256 checksum in the <a href="/methodology/">sample manifest</a> before comparing it with another mode.</p><h2>Plan a year of photographs.</h2><p>RAW uses this sample’s exact byte count. JPEG assumes <strong>8 MB per photograph</strong> for planning; replace that estimate in the calculator with your own file size. All values below are decimal GB, before backup copies.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Estimated annual photo storage — {camera.name}</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Photos / year</th><th scope="col">JPEG (8 MB estimate)</th><th scope="col">RAW (measured sample)</th><th scope="col">RAW + JPEG</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[1000,5000,10000,50000].map(count=><tr><th scope="row">{count.toLocaleString('en-US')}</th>{['jpeg','raw','both'].map(format=><td>{gb(estimate(count,format).annualGB)} GB</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p><a href="/cameras/">Compare measured files from other cameras</a> or open the <a href="/memory-card-calculator/">standalone memory card calculator</a>.</p><h2>Questions about this sample</h2>{camera.questions.map(q=><details><summary>{q.question}</summary><p>{q.answer}</p></details>)}</section>
<Calculator sampleId={camera.sampleId}/>
<section class="wrap related-guides"><p class="eyebrow">MORE CAMERA FIELD NOTES</p><div>{related.map(c=><a href={`/${samples.find(s=>s.id===c.sampleId)!.slug}-raw-vs-jpeg/`}>{c.name} <span>↗</span></a>)}</div></section>
</Layout>
